payload.description:
Operation body. Always a JSON object, never a JSON-encoded string. Copy the template for the chosen operation:
  property.set           {"layerId":"layer-1","property":"opacity","value":40}
  property.key.set       {"frame":12,"layerId":"layer-1","property":"opacity","value":40}
  property.key.remove    {"frame":12,"layerId":"layer-1","property":"opacity","value":40}
  property.animation.set {"animated":true,"layerId":"layer-1","property":"opacity"}
  history.undo           {}
  history.redo           {}
  diagnostics.replay     {"request":{"operation":"property.set","payload":{"layerId":"layer-1","property":"opacity","value":40}}}
`layerId` is `layers[].layerUid` from the latest snapshot. `property` is the `id` of a registered property capability (engineering/application/capabilities/*.json) — the payload key is `property` even though the descriptor names it `id`. `frame` defaults to the document's current frame wherever the template omits it.
